within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L04A_Immunosuppressants.L04AC18_Risankizumab;
model Risankizumab_Khatri2020_PD_pasi90
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Khatri_2020 :: PASI90 (PASI90)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0.616,      // [1]
    Emax = 0.812,  // [1]
    EC50 = 0.000441,  // [kg/m3; μg/mL × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 μg/mL per second
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 4.5, Interval = 0.009),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Risankizumab_Khatri2020_PD_pasi90</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Khatri A et al., <i>Clinical pharmacology and therapeutics 107(2):378–387</i> 2020 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/cpt.1594\">doi:10.1002/cpt.1594</a>) — PASI90 against risankizumab μg/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =      0.616          drug-free response (baseline) (Exponent for effect of baseline hs-CRP on EC50, Q324)
  Emax  =      0.812          maximal effect term (Emax, Q320)
  EC50  =      0.441 μg/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one μg/mL of risankizumab per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.616   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.441 μg/mL)  response 1.022
  exposure -> infinity  response 1.428</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Khatri_2020: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Risankizumab_Khatri2020_PD_pasi90;
